  This closes open item B12 as a QUESTION. It is not a shipped fix: it is a runtime
  monkeypatch verified on one kernel and one shape. What it establishes is that the
  remaining ~91% of the regression is a caching bug of the same kind as #24, in the
  same dispatch path, and that the upstream change is small — register the lowering
  once per compile-cache key instead of once per call.

